nevada's democratic attorney general  aaron ford also weighed in on how the  election has been handled  and what voters should expect moving  forward 8 news now reporter kate houston  is over in our newsroom with what the  attorney general had to say  kate brian attorney general ford spoke  directly to voters during a facebook  live interview with battleborn progress  and he tried to reassure nevadans that  their votes will be counted  throughout the interview ford touched on  many different topics one issue brought  up multiple times was voter fraud  ford says there is simply no evidence of  voter fraud nor  obstruction of the observation of the  voting process here in nevada  now as for the time it takes to deliver  election results  ford reminded voters that many nevadans  took advantage of the vote by mail  process that paired with the safeguards  in place to prevent fraud  means it could take longer to receive  results  listen we knew that the process will  take time but this process is working  and instead of our election officials  receiving condemnation  over the consternation related to count  voting we should be giving them  commendations because they're working  very hard and doing their  very best to ensure that we have an  accurate count  attorney general aaron ford went on to  say that politicians will not decide who  wins this election  it's the american voters who will decide  he wants the will of the people in  nevada to speak for itself  now this conversation also touched on  the vote counting process  and how signatures are validated and you  can reach out to the clark county  elections department for more  information on that reporting from the  newsroom kate houston back to you
 

